WEBVTT

00:34:26.884 --> 00:34:30.347
the working relationship is what helps
drive getting something done.

00:34:30.371 --> 00:34:32.595
AG: He excelled at listening
and collaborating,

00:34:32.619 --> 00:34:34.468
so they gave him a six-week trial.

00:34:34.492 --> 00:34:36.063
Scott learned new skills quickly

00:34:36.087 --> 00:34:38.162
and started opening up to his colleagues.

00:34:38.186 --> 00:34:40.932
At the end of the trial,
he was hired, and today --

00:34:40.956 --> 00:34:42.551
SK: I've been working for Menlo

00:34:42.575 --> 00:34:46.139
for five years, three months and 10 days.

00:34:46.163 --> 00:34:49.201
RS: And now he's one of our
most revered team members.

00:34:49.513 --> 00:34:50.821
AG: I didn't realize this,

00:34:50.845 --> 00:34:54.082
but I think part of the genius
of the way that you approach this

00:34:54.106 --> 00:34:57.004
is if you have people
working on multiple tasks

00:34:57.028 --> 00:34:58.496
with different partners,

00:34:58.520 --> 00:35:00.988
then you actually do get to find